@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms & Conditions | Karnel Travel Guide";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Draft terms for using Karnel Travel Guide, submitting travel inquiries and requesting bookings.";
}

<main class="policy-page">
    <header class="policy-hero">
        <div class="container policy-hero__inner">
            <nav class="policy-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
                <a href="@Url.Action("Index", "Home")">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Terms &amp; Conditions</span>
            </nav>
            <p class="policy-eyebrow">Policies &amp; information</p>
            <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
            <p class="policy-intro">These draft terms explain how Karnel Travel Guide may be used and how travel inquiries and booking requests are handled.</p>
            <p class="policy-status">Draft for business review. No effective or last-updated date has been assigned.</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container policy-layout">
        <aside class="policy-toc" aria-label="On this page">
            <p>On this page</p>
            <ol>
                <li><a href="#acceptance">Acceptance</a></li>
                <li><a href="#use">Website use</a></li>
                <li><a href="#inquiries">Inquiries and bookings</a></li>
                <li><a href="#listings">Listings and providers</a></li>
                <li><a href="#intellectual-property">Intellectual property</a></li>
                <li><a href="#responsibility">Responsibility</a></li>
                <li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
            </ol>
        </aside>

        <article class="policy-content">
            <section id="acceptance">
                <h2>1. Introduction and acceptance</h2>
                <p>Karnel Travel Guide is a travel information and inquiry platform focused on destinations, accommodation, transport, dining and travel experiences in Pakistan. By using this website, you agree to use it lawfully and respectfully.</p>
                <p>These are draft terms and require business approval before they are treated as the final terms governing customer relationships.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="use">
                <h2>2. Website use and customer responsibilities</h2>
                <p>You must provide information that is accurate, current and yours to submit. Do not misuse the website, interfere with its operation, attempt unauthorized access, submit harmful material, or use another person’s account or personal information.</p>
                <p>You are responsible for reviewing information before relying on it, keeping account credentials confidential, and promptly telling Karnel Travel Guide if you believe an account or booking record is incorrect.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="inquiries">
                <h2>3. Travel inquiries and booking requests</h2>
                <p>A contact inquiry is a request for information or assistance. A booking request contains proposed travel details for review. Neither is, by itself, a confirmed reservation or a guarantee that a service will be available.</p>
                <p>Booking requests are subject to the website’s configured availability, validation rules and review process. A request may be returned for clarification or may not be accepted. A booking becomes confirmed only when Karnel Travel Guide communicates confirmation through the applicable workflow.</p>
                <p>Where the website presents a demo payment flow, the payment is recorded as a simulated transaction. A successful demo payment can place a booking into an administrator-approval state; it is not evidence of a live payment gateway settlement or a confirmed third-party service.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="listings">
                <h2>4. Service descriptions and listing accuracy</h2>
                <p>Listings, descriptions, prices, images, dates and availability are provided for guidance and may change. The website aims to keep information useful, but customers should confirm material details before making travel decisions.</p>
                <p>Some information may be supplied by or relate to independent accommodation, transport, restaurant, tour or other travel providers. Their own terms, availability, safety standards and service conditions may apply.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="intellectual-property">
                <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
                <p>Unless stated otherwise, the website’s text, branding, layout, software and original materials belong to Karnel Travel Guide or are used with permission. You may view and use the website for personal travel planning, but you must not copy, reproduce, publish, sell or alter protected material without permission.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="responsibility">
                <h2>6. Limitation of responsibility</h2>
                <p>Travel involves changing conditions and decisions by independent providers. Information on this website is not a substitute for checking current requirements, provider terms, weather, road conditions, health guidance or other safety information.</p>
                <p>This draft does not attempt to exclude responsibilities that cannot lawfully be excluded. Any final limitation, liability wording, governing law or jurisdiction must be approved by the business and reviewed for the locations in which the service operates.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="changes">
                <h2>7. Changes and contact</h2>
                <p>The website may change its content, features and these draft terms. The final publication process should define how material changes will be communicated and when they take effect.</p>
                <p>For questions about these terms or a travel request, use the <a href="@Url.Action("Index", "Contact")">contact and inquiry page</a>. Business owners should confirm the legal business name, contact details, effective date, governing law and final approval before publication.</p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </div>
</main>
